<MainLayout
  title="Deadbolt Installation in Delaware | Deadbolt Upgrade & Replacement | 1st Capital Locksmith"
  description="Professional deadbolt installation in Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith installs and upgrades deadbolts for homes and businesses throughout Kent County — single-cylinder, double-cylinder, smart lock deadbolts, and high-security Grade 1 deadbolts. Call (302) 735-0050."
>

  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="bg-white border-b border-gray-200">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-3">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 flex-wrap">
        <li>
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Home</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <a href="/services/" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Services</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <span class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold">Deadbolt Installation</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Schema: Breadcrumbs -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Deadbolt Installation", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/deadbolt-installation/" }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: Service -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Deadbolt Installation in Delaware",
    "description": "Professional deadbolt installation, upgrade, and replacement services for residential and commercial properties throughout Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith installs single-cylinder, double-cylinder, smart lock, and high-security Grade 1 deadbolts.",
    "provider": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "1st Capital Locksmith",
      "telephone": "+13027350050",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "addressLocality": "Dover",
        "addressRegion": "DE",
        "addressCountry": "US"
      }
    },
    "areaServed": {
      "@type": "State",
      "name": "Delaware"
    },
    "serviceType": "Deadbolt Installation"
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: FAQ -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does deadbolt installation cost in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The cost of deadbolt installation depends on the type of deadbolt, the number of doors, and whether any door prep work is needed. We provide a clear upfront quote before any work begins. Call (302) 735-0050 for a fast estimate."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the best deadbolt for a front door?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "For most residential front doors, an ANSI Grade 1 single-cylinder deadbolt from a reputable brand like Schlage or Kwikset is the best choice. Grade 1 is the highest residential security rating and provides strong resistance against forced entry."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can you install a deadbolt on any door?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Most standard exterior doors can accommodate a deadbolt. If your door does not already have a deadbolt hole, we can drill and prep the door on-site. We'll inspect your door first and advise on the best option."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the difference between a single and double cylinder deadbolt?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A single-cylinder deadbolt uses a key on the outside and a thumb-turn on the inside — the most common type for exterior doors. A double-cylinder deadbolt requires a key on both sides, which prevents someone from breaking a nearby window and reaching in to unlock the door. Double-cylinder locks require extra care for fire safety since they need a key to exit."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you install smart lock deadbolts in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. We install keypad deadbolts, Z-Wave smart locks, Bluetooth smart locks, and other electronic deadbolt systems throughout Delaware. Call us and we'll confirm compatibility with your door and your preferred brand."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long does deadbolt installation take?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A standard deadbolt installation on a prepared door typically takes 20–30 minutes per lock. If the door requires boring (cutting a new hole), it takes a bit longer. We handle the entire job on-site at your property."
        }
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative min-h-[340px] md:min-h-[550px] flex items-center text-white py-10 md:py-20"
    style="background-image: url('/images/deadbolt-installation.jpg'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/72"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-6 z-10">
      <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-xs md:text-sm mb-2 md:mb-4">Deadbolt Installation Services — Delaware</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-3 md:mb-6 max-w-3xl leading-tight">
        Professional Deadbolt Installation in Delaware — Stronger Locks, Safer Homes
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm md:text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-5 md:mb-8">
        A deadbolt is your front door's most important line of defense against forced entry. 1st Capital Locksmith installs, upgrades, and replaces deadbolts for homeowners and businesses throughout Delaware — with quality hardware, expert installation, and upfront pricing every time.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <a
          href="tel:3027350050"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-bold text-base md:text-lg hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
        >
          Call (302) 735-0050
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact/"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-white px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-semibold text-sm md:text-base hover:bg-white hover:text-[#1A1F22] transition"
        >
          Get a Free Quote
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Bar -->
  <section class="bg-[#0E1B2F] py-8">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">All Door Types</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Front, Back, Side & Interior Doors</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Grade 1 Hardware</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Highest Residential Security Rating</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Mobile Service</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">We Come Directly to Your Property</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Upfront Pricing</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Clear Quote Before We Start</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Delaware's Deadbolt Installation Experts</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6 leading-snug">
            Deadbolt Installation & Upgrade Service Throughout Delaware
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your home or business relies on a spring latch or a worn-out old deadbolt for security, you're more vulnerable than you might think. A quality deadbolt — properly selected and correctly installed — is one of the single most effective steps you can take to harden your doors against break-in attempts. Studies consistently show that most burglars look for quick, easy entry, and a strong deadbolt significantly raises that barrier.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            1st Capital Locksmith provides professional deadbolt installation services for homes, apartments, rental properties, and commercial businesses throughout Delaware. We carry quality hardware from trusted brands and take the time to ensure every deadbolt is correctly fitted, aligned, and functioning smoothly before we leave your property.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Whether you need a basic single-cylinder deadbolt installed on a new door, a double-cylinder deadbolt added to a door with a window nearby, or a keypad or smart lock deadbolt for keyless entry convenience, we handle all types throughout Dover, Milford, Smyrna, Camden, Harrington, and all of Kent County, Delaware.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Photo Slot 1: Deadbolt installation in progress -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-[#F8F8F5] aspect-[4/3] flex items-center justify-center">
            <img
              src="/images/deadbolt-installation.jpg"
              alt="Professional deadbolt installation on a residential front door in Delaware"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
              width="600"
              height="450"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6">Our Deadbolt Installation Services Include:</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            {[
              "New Deadbolt Installation",
              "Deadbolt Upgrade & Replacement",
              "Single-Cylinder Deadbolt Installation",
              "Double-Cylinder Deadbolt Installation",
              "Keypad Deadbolt Installation",
              "Smart Lock Deadbolt Installation",
              "High-Security Grade 1 Deadbolt Installation",
              "Door Boring & Prep for New Deadbolts",
              "Deadbolt Strike Plate Reinforcement",
              "Residential & Commercial Deadbolt Service",
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-700">
                <span class="w-6 h-6 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
            <a
              href="tel:3027350050"
              class="w-full inline-flex justify-center items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 text-white font-bold hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
            >
              Call (302) 735-0050 Now
            </a>
        </div>        </div>      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Types of Deadbolts We Install</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">
          Deadbolt Installation Options in Delaware
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Not all deadbolts are created equal. Here's a detailed breakdown of every deadbolt type we install and the situations where each one is the right fit. Not sure what you need? Call us and we'll walk you through it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">

        <!-- Single Cylinder -->
        <div id="single-cylinder" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 118 0m-4 8v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Single-Cylinder Deadbolt Installation in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              The single-cylinder deadbolt is the most widely used deadbolt type for residential exterior doors throughout Delaware. It operates with a keyed cylinder on the outside and a simple thumb-turn on the inside, allowing you to lock and unlock quickly from inside without a key — important for emergency exit. This is the correct choice for the vast majority of front doors, back doors, and side entry doors.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              When selecting a single-cylinder deadbolt, quality and grade rating matter enormously. Cheap, builder-grade deadbolts sold at big-box stores are often ANSI Grade 3 — the lowest rating — and can be defeated surprisingly quickly. 1st Capital Locksmith recommends and installs ANSI Grade 1 deadbolts, which are the highest residential security rating and provide dramatically better resistance to picking, drilling, and forced entry.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We carry quality single-cylinder deadbolts in a range of finishes to match your existing hardware. Installation includes proper alignment with your door frame and strike plate reinforcement to ensure the bolt seats fully and the lock performs as designed.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Double Cylinder -->
        <div id="double-cylinder" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 15v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2zM10 7a2 2 0 114 0v3H10V7z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Double-Cylinder Deadbolt Installation in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A double-cylinder deadbolt requires a key to operate from both the outside and the inside. This makes it the right choice for doors that have glass panels, sidelights, or windows close enough that a burglar could break the glass, reach through, and turn a standard thumb-turn to unlock the door. With a double-cylinder lock, even getting a hand through the broken glass doesn't help — they still need the key.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Double-cylinder deadbolts come with an important safety consideration: in a fire or emergency, you need a key to exit. If you choose a double-cylinder deadbolt, we strongly recommend keeping a key hung near — but not reachable from — the door at all times, and making sure every household member knows where it is. Many homeowners use a key holder mounted a safe distance from the glass.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              1st Capital Locksmith installs double-cylinder deadbolts throughout Delaware and will walk you through the safety guidelines before completing the installation. Your security and your family's safe exit in an emergency are both priorities we take seriously.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Keypad Deadbolt -->
        <div id="keypad" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 3H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v4m6-6h10a2 2 0 012 2v4M9 3v18m0 0h10a2 2 0 002-2V9M9 21H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V9m0 0h18" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Keypad Deadbolt Installation in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Keypad deadbolts combine the security of a traditional deadbolt with the convenience of keyless entry. You unlock your door by entering a PIN code — no key needed. This is a practical solution for families where kids come home from school before parents, for vacation rental properties, for landlords managing tenant access, or for anyone who's tired of fumbling for keys.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Modern keypad deadbolts offer features like auto-locking after a set time, multiple user codes (so you can give different codes to different people and delete them individually when needed), and backup key entry. Many models also have a built-in alarm that triggers after repeated incorrect code attempts — a valuable feature that adds an extra layer of security.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              1st Capital Locksmith installs keypad deadbolts from trusted brands throughout Delaware. We handle everything from hardware selection through full installation and programming, and we make sure you're comfortable operating the lock before we leave.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Smart Lock Deadbolt -->
        <div id="smart-lock" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 18h.01M8 21h8a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H8a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Smart Lock Deadbolt Installation in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Smart lock deadbolts take keyless entry to the next level. They connect via Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, or Z-Wave to your smartphone and smart home system, allowing you to lock and unlock your door remotely, receive notifications when your door is locked or unlocked, grant temporary access codes to guests or contractors, and check the status of your lock from anywhere.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Popular smart lock deadbolt brands like Schlage Encode, Kwikset Halo, Yale Assure, and August Smart Lock all offer excellent security alongside their smart features. Many also integrate with Amazon Alexa, Google Home, and Apple HomeKit ecosystems. The important thing is making sure the lock is professionally installed so it operates correctly and securely — a misaligned smart lock can fail to engage properly despite showing as "locked" on your phone.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We install smart lock deadbolts throughout Delaware and ensure correct alignment, proper door prep, and full function testing before completing the job. Whether you already have a brand in mind or need a recommendation, call us and we'll help you find the right fit.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- High Security Deadbolt -->
        <div id="high-security" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">High-Security Grade 1 Deadbolt Installation in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              For homeowners and property owners who want the highest level of door security available, we install ANSI Grade 1 high-security deadbolts. ANSI Grade 1 is the top residential security classification, tested to withstand at minimum 250,000 open/close cycles and significant impact force. Brands like Schlage B60N, Kwikset 980, and Medeco Maxum are examples of Grade 1 hardware that deliver real, measurable protection.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              High-security deadbolts often feature hardened steel bolts, anti-drill pins, anti-pick security pins, and reinforced housings that make them dramatically more resistant to the most common forms of physical attack. Combined with a properly reinforced strike plate and long screws that anchor into the door frame's structural wood, a Grade 1 deadbolt installation represents the standard we recommend for all primary entry doors.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              If you're upgrading from a builder-grade lock or have concerns about the security of your property, this is the installation we'd recommend. 1st Capital Locksmith carries and installs Grade 1 deadbolts throughout Delaware — call us to discuss the right option for your specific door and situation.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Deadbolt Replacement -->
        <div id="replacement" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Deadbolt Replacement in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              If your existing deadbolt is stiff, difficult to turn, loose in the door, damaged from a break-in attempt, or simply old and worn out, it's time for a replacement. A deadbolt that's struggling to operate reliably isn't providing the protection you're counting on — and a failing lock has a way of completely giving out at the most inconvenient possible moment.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith handles deadbolt replacements throughout Delaware on the same visit. We remove the old hardware, inspect the door and frame for any damage or alignment issues that need to be addressed, install the new deadbolt correctly, and test the operation before we leave. In most cases a standard deadbolt replacement fits into an existing door prep hole with no additional drilling required.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Replacing an outdated or damaged deadbolt is also a great opportunity to upgrade your security level at the same time. If you're currently running a builder-grade lock, a replacement with a quality Grade 1 deadbolt makes a significant difference for a reasonable cost.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Strike Plate Reinforcement -->
        <div id="strike-plate" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20 7l-8-4-8 4m16 0l-8 4m8-4v10l-8 4m0-10L4 7m8 4v10M4 7v10l8 4" />
            </svg>
          </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Strike Plate Reinforcement in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Here's a security fact that surprises many homeowners: even the best deadbolt in the world can fail if it's secured with a weak strike plate. The strike plate is the metal piece mounted on the door frame that receives the deadbolt. Most builder-installed strike plates are thin, flimsy, and held in place with short 3/4-inch screws that only go into the door casing — not the structural framing behind it. A strong kick can split the door frame around these small screws in seconds.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Proper deadbolt installation always includes reinforcing the strike plate with heavy-duty hardware and 3-inch screws that penetrate through the door casing and deep into the jack stud behind it. This dramatically increases the kick resistance of your door — some studies suggest it can increase resistance to forced entry by 10x or more compared to a standard installation.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Every deadbolt installation we perform at 1st Capital Locksmith includes strike plate inspection and reinforcement as part of the job. We don't install a lock without ensuring the frame is equally secure — because a chain is only as strong as its weakest link.
            </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

